5
00:00:10.496 --> 00:00:15.432
(audience cheering)
What is up?

6
00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:16.667
How are you guys?

7
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:17.500
How are you?

8
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.430
Oh, great. We're so happy you're here.

9
00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.350
I'm so happy I'm here.

10
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.190
How are you?

11
00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.023
I'm good, honey.

12
00:00:22.023 --> 00:00:23.354
How are you?

13
00:00:23.354 --> 00:00:24.187
Great.

14
00:00:24.187 --> 00:00:26.050
How was your guys's Thanksgiving?

15
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:26.900
Mine was great.

16
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.030
And I had all of my daughter's family,

17
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.750
which is my family, and we just had a blast.

18
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.620
We spent three days together cooking and shopping

19
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.670
and just merriment.

20
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:39.570
Yeah, that's awesome.

21
00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:40.403
Right?

22
00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.370
As soon as Thanksgiving is over, my family,

23
00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.560
we just go straight to Christmas.

24
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.393
Oh, totally.

25
00:00:46.393 --> 00:00:48.580
I think, Ross, you like to do your Christmas tree, like,

26
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.413
on Thanksgiving.

27
00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:50.707
Yeah, last bite of turkey and then I'm like,

28
00:00:50.707 --> 00:00:52.140
"Let's go put up the tree."

29
00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.826
I'm just like you.

30
00:00:53.826 --> 00:00:54.659
(audience laughs)
Yeah.

31
00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:55.492
High five.

32
00:00:55.492 --> 00:00:56.890
Leo, how was your Thanksgiving?

33
00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:57.740
Mine was great.

34
00:00:57.740 --> 00:01:01.300
We hung out at my grandma's, watch football, had Turkey,

35
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.150
you know, all the Thanksgiving classics.

36
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.070
All the classics, all the trimmings.

37
00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:06.903
Yep.

38
00:01:06.903 --> 00:01:08.370
All right, well, let's kick this off

39
00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:13.370
with a toast with our friendly Christmas cocktail, Leo.

40
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:14.640
What have we go?

41
00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.180
We have Santa's Hat Shirley Temple.

42
00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.130
Now, you might be thinking,

43
00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:21.020
is this just an ordinary Shirley Temple?

44
00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.880
No, it's a Santa's Hat Shirley Temple.

45
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:23.775
Of course.

46
00:01:23.775 --> 00:01:24.608
Of course.
(audience laughs)

47
00:01:24.608 --> 00:01:26.660
You start off with a normal Shirley Temple.

48
00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.900
If you don't know what that is,

49
00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.576
you've been living under a rock, just kidding.

50
00:01:30.576 --> 00:01:31.780
(everyone laughs)

51
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.770
You mix together ginger ale, a splash of grenadine,

52
00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:38.170
a bunch of ice, and, of course, three cherries.

53
00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.730
So, here's a Christmas twist.

54
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:41.150
All you do is you take your glass

55
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.100
and you dip it in some sort of

56
00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:43.840
like frosting.
Oh.

57
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:46.450
Or a marshmallow cream, in this case,

58
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.260
we're using marshmallow cream.

59
00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.250
Oh, yum.
Let's just

60
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:51.650
get that rim all smothered in it.

61
00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.630
Okay, gotta get it all gooey.

62
00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:54.830
All right.

63
00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:56.144
Oh, it's stuck.

64
00:01:56.144 --> 00:01:57.050
(Ross and audience laugh)

65
00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.400
It really did get stuck.

66
00:01:58.400 --> 00:01:59.650
Yeah.

67
00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.703
But it's gonna be a good adhesive.

68
00:02:03.477 --> 00:02:05.290
It is.
That Santa's snow

69
00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.390
is gonna stick right on.

70
00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:07.980
Is this coconut?

71
00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:10.920
That is, yes, coconut flakes.

72
00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.960
Oh, so we're gonna roll it in the coconut

73
00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.848
and then it sticks to the rim, right?

74
00:02:14.848 --> 00:02:15.681
Mhmm.

75
00:02:15.681 --> 00:02:17.460
And that's, like, the fluffy part of Santa's hat.

76
00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:18.360
Oh, cute.

77
00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.828
(audience applauds)

78
00:02:21.828 --> 00:02:22.661
Oh.

79
00:02:22.661 --> 00:02:24.870
And then we get to drink the real one.

80
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.940
Cheers you guys.

81
00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:26.773
Look, you guys, and this

82
00:02:26.773 --> 00:02:27.606
is what it looks like-
Cheers.

83
00:02:27.606 --> 00:02:28.439
When it's all done.

84
00:02:28.439 --> 00:02:29.490
I love this. Oh wait.

85
00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:30.730
And then Leo, don't forget though,

86
00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:31.920
we put the candy cane in,

87
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.690
and don't forget the maraschino cherries.

88
00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:34.710
Of course not.

89
00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:35.730
Right here.

90
00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.322
(audience cheers)

91
00:02:38.322 --> 00:02:42.591
Cute, I love it.
Cheers guys.

92
00:02:42.591 --> 00:02:43.562
I love you, Leo.

93
00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.062
I love you, Rossy.

94
00:02:46.101 --> 00:02:47.268
That's good.

95
00:02:50.041 --> 00:02:52.270
That is so good.
Great.

96
00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.830
I got my daily spill

97
00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.059
when I go on the Drew Barrymore Show, but whatever.

98
00:02:56.059 --> 00:02:57.819
(Ross and audience laughs)
It happens, it happens.

99
00:02:57.819 --> 00:02:58.652
It happens.

100
00:02:58.652 --> 00:03:00.310
By the way, I'm going to adopt that.

101
00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.260
It happens.

102
00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.093
It happens.

103
00:03:02.093 --> 00:03:02.926
Yep.

104
00:03:02.926 --> 00:03:03.770
All right, well, while we sip on these,

105
00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.210
you want to do a little story with us?

106
00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.043
Of course, I'd love to.

107
00:03:06.043 --> 00:03:06.876
Okay, great.

108
00:03:06.876 --> 00:03:07.890
What do you think about this?

109
00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.590
Do you know who Martha Stewart is?

110
00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:10.423
Uh-huh. Yeah.

111
00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:11.640
Who is she?

112
00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.120
She's a chef and my favorite thing that she cooks

113
00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.030
is cookies.

114
00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:16.650
You know what, you're right.

115
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:17.960
You are so right.

116
00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.330
Okay, well, "Martha Stewart Living" reports

117
00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:23.460
on a new study that says if you decorate your house

118
00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.220
for the holidays, you might seem friendlier

119
00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.620
to your neighbors.

120
00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.210
They say the lights, the deer, the snowmen,

121
00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:34.290 line:15%
they all make it look like a friendly family lives inside.

122
00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.440 line:15%
What do you think about this?

123
00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.773 line:15%
I actually believe that theory because, one moment,

124
00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.050 line:15%
I actually believe that theory

125
00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.170 line:15%
because whenever I'm on the bus on my way to school

126
00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:46.190 line:15%
or back from school or I'm in my parents' car,

127
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:48.530 line:15%
I always see them going around, like,

128
00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.250 line:15%
straight after Thanksgiving through November 1st,

129
00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.280
I see them popping up everywhere,

130
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.420
and our town really goes out on Christmas decorations.

131
00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.380
And when I look at them, I think, wow,

132
00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.210
that person really took the time

133
00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:03.930
to decorate their house-
Aww.

134
00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.920
To make other people happy.

135
00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:06.753
Yeah.

136
00:04:06.753 --> 00:04:07.600
That's what I think.

137
00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.490
And then, if I'm in a bad mood or I'm in a good mood,

138
00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.480
that just makes my day even better.

139
00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:13.363
What do you think?

140
00:04:13.363 --> 00:04:14.983
I agree.
(audience applauds)

141
00:04:14.983 --> 00:04:16.227
That's the whole point, right?

142
00:04:16.227 --> 00:04:17.060
Yeah.

143
00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:17.893
It is.

144
00:04:17.893 --> 00:04:19.720
It's like a big welcome mat.

145
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:20.630
Yeah.
Yeah.

146
00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:23.180
It's either saying I just want to visually present you

147
00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.350
with joy or come on in.

148
00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:26.183
Yeah.

149
00:04:26.183 --> 00:04:28.891
And most of the time, it's come on in.

150
00:04:28.891 --> 00:04:29.724
(audience laughs)

151
00:04:29.724 --> 00:04:31.480
Well, we should test that theory, Leo.

152
00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.230
Let's just go knock on a bunch of doors

153
00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:34.251
and see what happens.

154
00:04:34.251 --> 00:04:35.177
(Ross and audience laugh)

155
00:04:35.177 --> 00:04:36.330
Okay. I'll do that.

156
00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.163
Okay.

157
00:04:37.163 --> 00:04:38.150
Well, we'll do it together.

158
00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.410
All right, listen.

159
00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:42.780
Everyone's favorite Christmas villain, can we think of it?

160
00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:43.916
Guess.

161
00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:44.749
Grinch.

162
00:04:44.749 --> 00:04:45.940
Grinch.
Grinch, yeah.

163
00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:46.773
It's Grinch.

164
00:04:46.773 --> 00:04:48.007
It's the Grinch.

165
00:04:48.007 --> 00:04:50.600
"Architectural Digest" actually reports

166
00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:54.200
that now, you can take a vacation in the Grinch's lair.

167
00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.260
It's a rental in Boulder, Utah

168
00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.550 line:15%
carefully designed to look just like his cave

169
00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:02.000 line:15%
and the signs outside say, "Leave now," and "Get lost,"

170
00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.820 line:15%
kind of the opposite of the welcome and come on in.

171
00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.240 line:15%
And inside, you'll find his furry green shoes

172
00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.240 line:15%
and the fantastical organ.

173
00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.290 line:15%
What do you think, Leo?

174
00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:13.250 line:15%
Would you come on in or go away?

175
00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.580 line:15%
Well, on one condition, I'd come in,

176
00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.380 line:15%
and I think you all might agree with me.

177
00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.830 line:15%
As long as the Grinch is somewhere else,

178
00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:22.663 line:15%
doesn't matter

179
00:05:22.663 --> 00:05:24.510 line:15%
if it's the North Pole
(audience laughs)

180
00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.583 line:15%
or somewhere else, he just needs to be out of there.

181
00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.610 line:15%
If he is in a grumpy spirit,

182
00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:32.880 line:15%
he needs to be out of there

183
00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.870 line:15%
because I do not want him going around ruining my Christmas,

184
00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:38.058 line:15%
judging me what to do.
Thank you.

185
00:05:38.058 --> 00:05:41.058 line:15%
(audience applauds)

186
00:05:43.665 --> 00:05:44.880
Preach.

187
00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.770
I was paddle boarding, kayaking with my daughter.

188
00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:53.080
We went to San Diego and the guy literally goes,

189
00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:54.500
I was like, "That's such a cool house,"

190
00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.713
and he goes, "Oh, that's Theodor Geisel's house."

191
00:05:56.713 --> 00:05:57.720
I was like, "Dr. Seuss?"

192
00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:01.640
He goes, "Yeah, and his wife owned a house up on the hill

193
00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:04.350
because every holiday, she would get so upset

194
00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.770
about the holidays that she would just go

195
00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.330
to the house on the hill and avoid everyone,

196
00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:10.610
and that was the inspiration for the Grinch."

197
00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:11.610
Really?
Oh.

198
00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:12.493
Yes, put that in your-
I never knew,

199
00:06:12.493 --> 00:06:13.980
I would've never known.

200
00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.410
I never knew that either.

201
00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:18.360
Put that in your "Architectural Digest" article.

202
00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.230
Well, Leo, as always,

203
00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:23.040
we've been on this show together since the very beginning,

204
00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.960
and as long as we are here, I'd really like to be together,

205
00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.060
would that be okay?

206
00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:27.939
Yes.

207
00:06:27.939 --> 00:06:28.772
Thank you, Leo.
Cheers.

208
00:06:28.772 --> 00:06:29.605
Aww.

209
00:06:29.605 --> 00:06:31.061
(audience applauds)

210
00:06:31.061 --> 00:06:32.978
Everybody, Leo Kelly,

211
00:06:34.043 --> 00:06:34.876 line:15%
and if you'd like the recipe

212
00:06:35.963 --> 00:06:37.960 line:15%
to Santa's Hat Shirley Temple,

213
00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.473 line:15%
it's on our website.

214
00:06:40.604 --> 00:06:43.187 line:15%
(upbeat music)

